---
name: Update LLM Info
description: Add the newest models of a provider to packages/llm-info
version: 3
---

Update this repository with current information about large language models for
the named providers.

The data lives in `packages/llm-info`, its own npm package (`@tnt/llm-info`), with
one file of model entries per provider under `packages/llm-info/src/providers/`
(`gemini.ts`, `openai.ts`, `ollama.ts`, `anthropic.ts`, `mistral.ts`, ...).
Read the field definitions from `packages/llm-info/src/types.ts` instead of
assuming them — `LlmInfo` carries `model`, `displayName`, `description`,
`contextLength`, `maxCompletionTokens`, `regex`, `chatTemplate`, `mediaTypes` and
`recommendedFor`, and it has gained fields before.

Work one step at a time.

## 1. View the current information

Use the `Read` tool on the provider file (e.g.
`packages/llm-info/src/providers/gemini.ts`). If no file-reading tool is
available, say so and stop.

## 2. Fetch the new information

Use `WebSearch` to find the provider's current model list and `Fetch` to read the
page. Known mappings:

- `gemini`: <https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/models> —
  `maxCompletionTokens` is published as the output token limit, `contextLength`
  as the input token limit.

For a provider not listed, search for "latest <provider> models" and pick the most
authoritative page. If a tool is missing, stop and say which one.

Notes on what to record:

- Ignore models with no text output. This client consumes text (and optionally
  image) input and text output, so other capabilities add no value here.
- When a provider ships Experimental/Preview variants, maintain the newest dated
  one.
- Prefer the vendor's own numbers over a summary site.

## 3. Update the file

Use `Edit` (or `MultiEdit` for several entries in one pass) on the provider file.

- Do not delete an existing model. If one looks obsolete, say so in the summary
  and leave it in place.
- Avoid rewriting values that are already right; this step is about new models
  and missing fields.
- Stop and ask before any change that is nuanced, bulk, or a notable correction.

Afterwards, summarize what was added and what was left alone.

## 4. Publishing

Remind me that `@tnt/llm-info` needs a release. The chain is the
**Release @tnt/llm-info** workflow, which runs semantic-release through
`reusable-release.yml` and currently skips until the `SEMANTIC_RELEASE_*`
repository secrets exist. Do not commit, tag or publish on your own.

